instructions:
You are working in the dayjs repository checked out at /dayjs. Make ONLY the single change described below; do not touch any other file, and do not modify or delete any existing test file permanently.

GOAL: fix a bug in the timezone plugin.

STEP 1 (BASELINE, do this first, before editing anything):
  cd /dayjs && npx jest --coverage=false 2>&1 | tail -n 300 > /tmp/baseline_jest.txt
  cd /dayjs && npx jest --coverage=false 2>&1 | grep -E '^(Tests:|Test Suites:)|^FAIL' > /tmp/baseline_summary.txt
Record which test suites/tests fail at baseline (there may be none).

STEP 2 (THE FIX): edit /dayjs/src/plugin/timezone/index.js. The static function currently reads:

  d.tz = function (input, timezone) {
    const previousOffset = tzOffset(+d(), timezone)
    const localTs = d.utc(input).valueOf()
    const [targetTs, targetOffset] = fixOffset(localTs, previousOffset, timezone)
    const ins = d(targetTs).utcOffset(targetOffset)
    return ins
  }

It must become:

  d.tz = function (input, timezone) {
    if (typeof input !== 'string') {
      return d(input).tz(timezone)
    }
    const previousOffset = tzOffset(+d(), timezone)
    const localTs = d.utc(input).valueOf()
    const [targetTs, targetOffset] = fixOffset(localTs, previousOffset, timezone)
    const ins = d(targetTs).utcOffset(targetOffset)
    return ins
  }

Everything else in the file (and the string code path) must stay byte-identical. Do not reformat the file.

STEP 3 (VERIFY THE BUG IS FIXED): create a TEMPORARY test file /dayjs/test/plugin/__tz_repro.test.js with exactly this content:

